      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "Summer has flattened into that familiar NHL hush, but Toronto's work is already visible - less in the quiet than in the pile of new names. <strong>Gavin McKenna's gratitude for representing the Yukon has become the freshest hook of the offseason</strong>, a reminder that the future is the point now. The Maple Leafs finished 32-36-14 and 8th in the Atlantic, and that record has forced a hard reset rather than a polish job. Sergei Bobrovsky gives them a new backbone in goal, while McKenna's arrival opens a camp battle that could be the most intriguing thing in town when September finally wakes up. There is cap room, there is turnover, and there is no excuse for drifting. <strong>Training camp will tell whether this roster has been repaired - or merely rearranged</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated August 1, 2026"
      },
