      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "A club can feel two ways at once - buried in the standings, yet suddenly harder to dismiss. <strong>Toronto's 3-1 win over the Cardinals on Friday night</strong> gave the Blue Jays a second straight victory and a little late-summer bite, but it did not wash away the larger picture: 51-59, fifth in the AL East, 13.5 games back. Luis Urías delivered the decisive blow with a tiebreaking two-run single in the eighth, exactly the sort of bench punch a drifting season needs. The bigger question remains the deadline, and the recent wins won't change that calculus much. Still, a team that had been wobbling has found a pulse. <strong>Next up: the Cardinals again at 3:07 PM ET on Saturday, with Toronto trying to turn a brief spark into something sturdier.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated August 1, 2026"
      },
