      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "Quiet has become the Raptors' loudest sound - and that suits a club still waiting on the last pieces to click. <strong>The biggest development is the announced 2026 training camp and preseason schedule</strong>, a firm calendar that finally gives this offseason some shape. Toronto sits at 42-32 and 3rd in the Atlantic Division, but the real business now is roster construction, not box scores. The Kawhi Leonard saga still hangs over the summer, while the summer cupboard has also thinned with Christian Koloko landing a one-year deal with New Orleans. Scottie Barnes remains the organizing force, and everything the Raptors do from here will be about fitting the right veterans and young legs around him. <strong>Camp in Quebec City will tell us whether the next move is minor housekeeping or something far bolder.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated August 1, 2026"
      },
