    "article": {
      "title": "Saturday's Skate",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The Leafs are deep into a reshaped offseason, with NHL.com saying Gavin McKenna, the No. 1 pick in the 2026 NHL Draft, will get every chance to earn a top-six job in camp, while John Chayka has made defense a stated priority. Sportsnet also reports McKenna is proud to represent the Yukon, a neat detail for a prospect who could be part of the opening-night picture against Montreal on Sep. 29.",
        "The Blue Jays handled the Cardinals 3-1 last night, then turn right back around for a 3:07 PM ET first pitch on Sportsnet, with trade-deadline caution still hanging over a 51-59 club in fifth place in the AL East. The Raptors remain in deep offseason mode ahead of Oct. 3 against Miami, with chatter around the league still centering on the Clippers and Leonard investigation.",
        "For Washington, training camp is the story now: the Commanders open at Philadelphia on Sep. 13, and camp reports say Dan Quinn's focus on competition is already showing up in the building. One camp note worth watching today is which early standouts keep turning heads as the roster starts to sort itself out."
      ]
